WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.270
We've been chatting with the one and only, Ted Danson,

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.960
who's back in the new season of NBC's "Mr. Mayor."

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.240
All right, let's get back to it.

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.740
Is it possible to get Ted's take,

5
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.250
like you could, in a sentence, tell us your take on blank?

6
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.083
Yes.

7
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:16.320
Perfect, okay.
(audience laughs)

8
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.189
Here we go, everybody. It's Ted's take!

9
00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:20.620
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

10
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.470
Okay, your take on love.

11
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.800
Wow, well, if you're blessed to have love...

12
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.350
To be able to love someone and be loved in return

13
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.720
is really, to me, the reason why we're human beings.

14
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.590
It is the, it's heaven on earth.

15
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.663
I love that. Work!

16
00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.750
I don't have any wisdom.

17
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.870
The reason why I'm still working at 74

18
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.400
is 'cause I love to go to work.

19
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.760
I love to drive through studio gates.

20
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.290
I love to turn right on James Stewart Avenue

21
00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.700
and cross over Gregory Peck Street,

22
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.020
and show up at a studio and be surrounded by crew members

23
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.223
who you grow to adore over the years.

24
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.140
Yeah, I love going to work.

25
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.480
And I don't know if it defines me,

26
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.803
but it sure enriches my life.

27
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.800
Okay.
(audience applauds)

28
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.490
Amazing, and you are up there with those great gentlemen

29
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:20.260
that you just said, Peck and Stewart and Danson.

30
00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.230
Family.

31
00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.610
Family, wow.

32
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.430 line:15%
Mary and I both, what brings us literally the most joy

33
00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:33.080 line:15%
is when we sit down to a table of 12 people now with kids,

34
00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:38.080
grandkids, wives, spouses, boyfriends, 12 people,

35
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.450
and we sit down and we're surrounded by family,

36
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.503
brings us so much joy.

37
00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.240
I don't know what to say. It's such a blessing.

38
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.703
I don't have anything wise to say except thank you.

39
00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:50.040
No, the 12 people,

40
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.350
that painted the perfect storytelling picture.

41
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.650
I love it.

42
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.333
The one rule you live by.

43
00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.230
Be kind, yeah.

44
00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.373
Be kind to people.

45
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:05.150
Life can be scary and hard and tough

46
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.923
and all of that, so be kind.

47
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.170
Yes, that is perfect, perfect wisdom

48
00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.092
from you.
(audience applauds)

49
00:02:13.092 --> 00:02:15.900
Do you think that if they came to you

50
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.223
with like a "Cheers" reboot that you would ever do it?

51
00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.810
I'm positive we would not.

52
00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.080
(audience laughs)

53
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.660
First off, I think our creators,

54
00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.800
Jimmy Burrows, Les and Glen Charles, wouldn't want it.

55
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.760
They'd like to rest on their laurels, I'm sure.

56
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.510
But here's what it would look like.

57
00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.007
It'd be a bunch of old people sitting around the bar going,

58
00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:41.199
"What? What'd you say?

59
00:02:41.199 --> 00:02:42.032
(audience laughs)

60
00:02:42.032 --> 00:02:43.960
A horse walks into a what?"

61
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:47.360
(laughs) You know?

62
00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.550
I think there would be an appetite for it,

63
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:53.060 line:15%
but I'm just gonna watch the reruns for now.

64
00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.520 line:15%
And thank you for just being kind enough

65
00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.470 line:15%
to put yourself out there on all these incredible shows,

66
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.771 line:15%
so that we can watch you, Ted Danson.

67
00:03:01.771 --> 00:03:02.604
(audience applauds)

68
00:03:02.604 --> 00:03:04.210
You can watch "Mr. Mayor" Tuesdays

69
00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.130
at 8:30 Eastern on NBC.

70
00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.530
Ted, I love you so much.

71
00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:10.990
Thank you for being you.
Yeah,

72
00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.918
I love you, too, Drew.

73
00:03:11.918 --> 00:03:13.085
Ah!
I love you, too.

74
00:03:13.085 --> 00:03:14.895
I'm so glad you have this show.

75
00:03:14.895 --> 00:03:17.812 line:15%
